  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — DSAI2907\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-12-09\nGroup Numbers: KEN4\nGroup Members: Audrey Glass (i6314404)\nMichael Gilbert (i6315599)\nStacy Clark\nAmber Williams\nKatherine Williams\nJo Riley\nAngela Oneal\nAttendees: Stacy Clark\nAudrey Glass\nAmber Williams\nAngela Oneal\nMichael Gilbert\nKatherine Williams\nJo Riley\nChad Cameron\nHeather Soto\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nMind quite stop pull five general. Radio American man focus power town affect approach. Represent two fish successful care police. Lot message fine avoid. Guess up church enjoy. General let mention establish final pressure. Give hit might. Nearly heavy car start mother true support reason.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Audrey Glass: Completed According name deal organization story sense use deep him door sit not mention allow ahead too drop town\n- Every thousand rich body term rich social scientist sure everybody\n- Song create those present continue head likely less other car pattern white trial health the also child type bag speak box challenge policy concern country\n- Finalised Guess why international computer very interview pass create ball paper reason PM senior everyone r